Design: read the stream in a pull-based fashion. State machine:
1. First Read: read the 3-byte header, validate magic (0x4F 0x44), else "invalid header"; validate version 0x01, else "unsupported version".
2. Read loop: read 4-byte length. If length == 0 → sentinel. Then read 32-byte HMAC, compare with computed HMAC over all chunk bytes (including their 4-byte length prefixes — "all bytes between header and sentinel" = raw chunk encoding). If mismatch → error containing "integrity". Done.
3. Otherwise: read `length` bytes; parse nonce (first 12), ciphertext+tag (rest). Validate length >= 12+16? Length must be at least nonce+tag, i.e., 28 bytes, otherwise malformed → error. GCM open. Append to output buffer.

